Assignments (1):
Customer Discovery Pitch
[CANVAS]
Your task is to deliver a 3-minute pitch that pulls together and shares what you have learned from your customer discovery process. This is not a pitch of your solution—it’s a pitch of your insights. In this presentation, you will clearly communicate the most important problems, needs, or pain points you uncovered, explain how you validated them with real conversations, and show how your understanding of the opportunity has evolved.
The focus is on evidence-driven insights, not assumptions, and on demonstrating how talking with potential customers or stakeholders has shaped your thinking.
Deliverable: You should upload your slide deck to this assignment as a .pdf file with the naming convention: TeamNumber-CustomerDiscoveryPitch.pdf by Tuesday, October 6th at 11:59pm. Teams will give their live pitch in groups on Wednesday, October 7th. You'll have 3 minutes for your pitch, followed by 2 minutes of questions/feedback from the audience. 
Requirements
Time Limit: 3-minutes maximum. You will be cut off at the time limit.
Your pitch should address:
Who you talked to – Briefly describe the customer segments or stakeholders you interviewed/surveyed.
How many and how – Share the scope of your discovery (e.g., number of interviews, methods used).
Key insights – What problems, needs, or motivations did you uncover?
Evidence/examples – Use quotes, patterns, or stories from your discovery work to support your claims.
Implications – How these insights shape or reshape your understanding of the problem and potential opportunity.
Format:
Speak clearly and confidently.
Slides can include visuals, charts, or brief key points.
No reading from scripts—pitch should feel natural and conversational.
We do not recommend having more than 2 team members pitch. By the end of the semester all team members must pitch at least once. 




